/target/
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
/sbom.json
.continue/

# The mdBook build output. The book's source is docs/ itself (see docs/book.toml
# and docs/architecture/wiki-structure-and-publication.md); the rendered site is
# a build artifact, never committed. With src = "." mdBook writes the rendered
# index.html next to the sources as well as into the book directory.
/docs/book/
/docs/index.html

# A real configuration file is deployment-specific and may hold secrets. The
# service never creates one, so anything matching these is one an operator
# wrote; it belongs on the deployment, not in a commit. The documented template
# is docs/deployment/config.example.json, which is committed.
/tucano-config.json
/*.config.json

# `docker compose` loads `.env` automatically from this directory. It holds the
# JWT signing secret and the bootstrap password, so it belongs on the machine,
# not in a commit. The committed template is .env.example.
/.env
